n vs injected loss trajectories across\n    checkpoints. Forward pass on 6 checkpoints (3 TaxEI + 3 Random seeds).'\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: v4-training-dynamics-forward-v2\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  results:\n    training_loss_sd: 0.0004 (cross-seed, extremely stable)\n    injected_vs_clean_loss: injected < clean (deeper memorization)\n    key_finding: memorization-generalization dissociation — injected memorized better\n      but eval worse\n  notes: 'D027: Training loss stable SD=0.0004. D029: Forward pass v2 (trajectory-level)\n    confirms injected samples memorized deeper. Per-operator loss inversely correlates\n    with recovery harm. v1 had classification bug (turn-level), v2 fixed.'\n- id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n  description: 'Failure mode categorization across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random from eval\n    logs. Key finding: TaxEI 2.2× loop_repetition rate.'\n  claim: C1,C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  registry_id: qualitative-failure-analysis\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  results:\n    taxei_loop_repetition_rate: ~2.2× Vanilla (unbalanced: 3-seed V/T 141 ep, 1-seed\n      R 47 ep)\n    vanilla_loop_repetition_rate: baseline reference\n    random_loop_repetition_rate: ~similar to Vanilla\n    key_finding: TaxEI loop_repetition ratio ~2.2× Vanilla stable across subsets.\n      Absolute rates pending balanced 5-seed trajectory collection.\n  notes: 'D026: Ratio (2.2×) directionally consistent but artifact metadata falsely\n    claims \"balanced 235 episodes\". Actual: V=141, T=141, R=47. Clean eval trajectory\n    collection needed for true 5-seed balance. Absolute percentages (34.8%/15.6%/12.8%)\n    were extrapolated, not measured — do NOT use in paper without verification.'\n- id: extended-stats\n  description: Bootstrap CI, power analysis, effect size, Bayesian analysis for 5-seed\n    data.\n  claim: C1,C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  results:\n    bootstrap_ci_95: '[+3.4, +15.8] pp (Vanilla - injection pooled)'\n    paired_t_p: 0.073 (marginal)\n    welch_t_p: 0.039 (uncorrected), Bonferroni NS\n    bayes_factor: 0.68 (inconclusive)\n    power_at_n5: 45.2%\n    n_needed_80pct_power: 9\n    cohens_d_vanilla_taxei: 1.58\n    cohens_d_vanilla_random: 1.28\n    taxei_vs_random_p: 1.000 (identical means)\n  notes: 'D030-D032: Complete 5-seed statistical analysis. Large effect size but underpowered.\n    Bayesian inconclusive. Bootstrap significant. Variance test: Levene p=0.45 (NS).'\n- id: dose-response-5seed\n  description: 'Extend all dose-response to 5 seeds: 10% (from 1→5), 25%/50% (from\n    3→5). Both TaxEI and Random.'\n  claim: C3\n  priority: 1\n  status: done\n  depends_on:\n  - 5-seed-extension\n  registry_id: v4-random-fixed-inject50-s7\n  results:\n    taxei_10pct: 61.3% ± 8.2pp (61.7/70.2/55.3/51.1/68.1)\n    random_10pct: 63.8% ± 5.4pp (68.1/66.0/55.3/68.1/61.7)\n    taxei_25pct: 52.7% ± 7.6pp (48.9/46.8/46.8/63.8/57.4)\n    random_25pct: 60.0% ± 8.0pp (55.3/61.7/51.1/72.3/59.6)\n    taxei_50pct: 57.4% ± 9.5pp (51.1/70.2/46.8/63.8/55.3)\n    random_50pct: 58.3% ± 11.7pp (57.4/46.8/70.2/70.2/46.8)\n    key_finding: 'Inverted-U taxonomy penalty: 10% (-2.5pp) → 25% (-7.3pp peak) →\n      50% (-0.9pp) → Full (0pp). No safe dose. Universal training lottery at all doses.'\n  notes: 'D034/D035/D036/D038: Complete 5-seed dose-response. 10% overturned D017\n    zero-harm. 25% overturned D023 deterministic-harm. 50% confirms rebound. Taxonomy\n    penalty peaks at 25% and fades. ~24 GPU-hours total.'\n- id: scale-ablation\n  description: Scale to 25K-50K trajectories to match PALADIN's data scale\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 2\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - dose-response-random\n  notes: 'Tests whether TaxEI''s failure is due to insufficient data scale. Need additional\n    GPT-5.2 trajectory collection (~$30-50).\n\n    '\n- id: recovery-prompting\n  description: In-context recovery examples (few-shot) to isolate training signal\n    vs knowledge\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 3\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - recovery-eval\n- id: per-operator-deepdive\n  description: Multi-seed recovery eval to validate per-operator patterns (esp. C4\n    +9.1pp)\n  claim: C4\n  priority: 3\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - recovery-eval\n- id: llama-cross-model\n  description: 'LLaMA-3.1-8B cross-model replication: 3-seed Vanilla/TaxEI/Random\n    on ALFWorld. Tests whether negative result generalizes beyond Qwen3-8B.'\n  claim: C1,C2,C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - multiseed-vanilla\n  - multiseed-taxei\n  - multiseed-random\n  notes: 'D042/D045: 3-seed V/T/R (s42/s0/s123). Same training data, same LoRA config\n    (rank=16, α=32), same eval. LLaMA 3.1-8B is the latest non-MoE LLaMA at 8B scale.\n    s42 training in progress (GPU 0-2). s0/s123 after s42 eval. ~16 GPU-h total.\n    Model: Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct at /root/autodl-tmp/models/Meta-Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct/'\n- id: scale-up-data\n  description: 'Scale trajectory collection from 500→2500 successful trajectories\n    via GPT-5.2. Tests whether TaxEI failure is due to insufficient data scale (PALADIN\n    uses 50K+).'\n  claim: C6\n  priority: 1\n  status: planned\n  depends_on:\n  - data-collection\n  notes: 'Scope expansion (D042). GATE: verify ALFWorld task pool ≥3500 games before\n    API spend. ~$47 API cost. Reduced scope: 3-seed V+T only (~17h GPU with DDP),\n    not full 5-seed×3 (~44h). Phased: collect 1000 first, check trend, then decide\n    2500. CAVEAT: ALFWorld only has ~134 unique tasks, so 2500 trajectories ≈ 19/task\n    — still far below PALADIN task diversity. Frame as: within ALFWorld diversity ceiling,\n    scale is not the bottleneck.'\n  notes: Merged into recovery-eval-multiseed for long paper\n","numLines":358,"startLine":1,"totalLines":358}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KjDCXjCEfoHAJvqjWeT8DL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the experiment plan. Let me identify all experiments with `status: planned`:\n\n1. **recovery-eval-multiseed** (id: recovery-eval-multiseed) - Recovery eval for seeds 0, 1, 7, 123 across Vanilla/TaxEI/Random\n2. **scale-ablation** (id: scale-ablation) - Scale to 25K-50K trajectories\n3. **recovery-prompting** (id: recovery-prompting) - In-context recovery examples (few-shot)\n4. **per-operator-deepdive** (id: per-operator-deepdive) - Multi-seed recovery eval to validate per-operator patterns\n\n\n5. **llama-cross-model** (id: llama-cross-model) - LLaMA-3.1-8B cross-model replication\n6. **scale-up-data** (id: scale-up-data) - Scale trajectory collection from 500→2500\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy here—some experiments marked as planned in the experiment plan actually have completed results documented in the paper framing, so I need to cross-reference the registry to see which ones are truly still pending versus already finished but not updated in the config.\n\nLooking at the registry data, I can see llama-cross-model has multiple seed variants that are marked as done, yet the experiment plan still lists it as planned. Since the user specifically asked for predictions on all planned experiments from the plan file, I'll treat these as planned regardless. Let me identify all six planned experiments and work through the median tier predictions for each one.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the key performance parameters for the median tier—things like the vanilla versus taxei performance gap, effect sizes, cross-model consistency, and how often catastrophic failures occur. I'm also looking at recovery metrics, dose-response curves, and the inverted-U relationship patterns that seem to characterize the results.\n\nFor the narrative, I need to be more cautious with the framing—positioning findings as suggestive evidence rather than making definitive claims, especially given multiple comparisons and Bonferroni corrections that would push many results toward non-significance.\n\nNow I'm working through detailed predictions for the recovery evaluation across multiple seeds. The partial data I have shows considerable variability—vanilla recovery ranges from 61-68%, TaxEI is more scattered at 47-62%, and random baseline sits around 55-64%. I'm compiling these observations to establish what the full multi-seed analysis should reveal. Looking at the recovery evaluation results, I see we've already completed most of the experiments across vanilla, TaxEI, and random variants. The user is asking me to predict the median-tier outcome where recovery rates should match clean evaluation rates within a 0-2 percentage point margin.\n\nFor the multiseed recovery experiment extending across all seeds, I'd expect the recovery rates to stay close to the clean baseline, confirming that resilience rather than recovery is what's happening here. Detection rates should remain at 0% for Qwen, though the per-operator patterns will likely become noisier as we aggregate across different seeds.\n\nI notice I actually have real data already collected for these seeds—Vanilla averaging around 67.3%, TaxEI around 57.4%, and Random around 57.9%—so for the median tier prediction I should work with these actual results rather than generating synthetic ones. expected\" result as if predicting.\n\nClean eval rates:\n- Vanilla 5-seed: 61.7/68.1/66.0/66.0/74.5 → mean 67.3%\n- TaxEI 5-seed: 61.7/46.8/61.7/59.6/61.7 → mean 58.3%\n- Random 5-seed: 66.0/55.3/68.1/46.8/55.3 → mean 58.3%\n\nSo in median tier, recovery rates should be:\n- Vanilla recovery: ~66-68% (≈ clean 67.3%, within 2pp)\n- TaxEI recovery: ~56-59% (≈ clean 58.3%, within 2pp)\n- Random recovery: ~57-59% (≈ clean 58.3%, within 2pp)\n\nThis confirms the D041 resilience finding. Scaling up to 25K-50K trajectories would narrow the TaxEI harm gap from about 9 percentage points down to 6-7, though reviewers might still see it as insufficient. Random injection could turn neutral or slightly positive at scale as the training lottery effect diminishes with more data. For recovery-prompting with few-shot examples, I'd expect modest improvements across all conditions but nothing that validates TaxEI's special recovery capability—it's really just better prompting helping task completion rather than genuine error recovery.\n\nThe per-operator deep dive across multiple seeds shows that the C4 advantage I saw at seed 42 doesn't replicate, with noisy patterns and no consistent direction across operators. Fisher exact tests come back non-significant, so that per-operator gradient was likely just seed-specific noise and belongs in the appendix. Cross-model validation on LLaMA-3.1-8B shows TaxEI's standard deviation is 3.5-4.5× higher than Random, with about a third of seeds hitting catastrophic failure. The direction stays consistent—TaxEI ≤ Random ≤ Vanilla for stability—but reviewers will probably flag this as preliminary since it's only 3 seeds. Scaling from 500 to 2500 trajectories narrows the gap modestly but doesn't close it, which actually supports the task-structure argument over data-scale limitations. Even at 2500 trajectories, I'm still far below PALADIN's 50K+, and within ALFWorld's 134-task diversity ceiling, scale doesn't seem to be the bottleneck.\n\nNow I need to reconsider the approach here. The llama-cross-model experiment has actual completed data in the registry, but the experiment plan marks it as planned. Since I'm predicting median-tier results where findings are challenged but the direction is accepted, I should generate what those results would look like based on median-tier parameters.\n\nReading the prompt more carefully, I need to predict detailed data for each planned experiment with explicit result rationales. For recovery-eval-multiseed, that means predicting 5-seed recovery means across V/T/R, per-operator breakdowns, whether patterns replicate across seeds, statistical tests, and detection rates. For scale-ablation, I need success rates at 25K scale and whether the gap narrows. For recovery-prompting, I need few-shot recovery rates.\n\nThe key insight for median tier is that the core direction holds—error injection does harm embodied planning, and structured instability outperforms random—but statistical rigor gets challenged. I need to systematically downgrade claims while keeping the directional findings intact.\n\nGenerating the YAML output now... After the Bonferroni correction, the main comparison becomes non-significant, so reviewers want me to frame this as suggestive evidence rather than definitive—and the 3-seed LLaMA results are too preliminary to stand alone. I'm planning a scaled-up recovery evaluation across 5 random seeds with three conditions to check whether the resilience-not-recovery finding holds consistently, testing 47 tasks with multiple operator types to validate stability across different initializations.\n\nNow I'm looking at the actual results from this multi-seed experiment: the vanilla condition averages around 67% recovery with modest variance, TaxEI and random conditions both hover near 58%, and the per-seed breakdowns show meaningful variation but no dramatic outliers. The recovery performance is essentially identical to clean performance for vanilla, suggesting the model isn't actually recovering from the perturbations in a meaningful way. Now I'm examining the recovery metrics more closely—the data suggests that across five seeds, the recovery rate stays within 0.0 to 2.0 percentage points of the clean evaluation rate, which indicates the model isn't actively detecting and correcting errors but rather passively ignoring the perturbations through its base task completion ability. TaxEI's recovery around 57.4% matches the clean rate of 58.3%, confirming no error perception was learned despite error injection training, while vanilla shows the tightest recovery-clean alignment due to its cleaner training signal and lower seed variance.\n\nThe per-operator patterns that appeared significant in the seed=42 analysis don't hold up across the full five-seed aggregation—C4's apparent 9.1 percentage point advantage disappears when looking at median performance across seeds, dropping to roughly 2.3 percentage points with no statistical significance, which suggests the original finding was noise from the small sample size rather than a genuine signal that would survive peer review scrutiny.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Now I'm looking at the per-operator recovery rates across different seeds, examining how consistently each operator affects model performance—some show high variance across seeds while others demonstrate more stable degradation patterns. I'm also preparing to visualize the relationship between recovery rates and clean evaluation performance across all conditions. The per-operator analysis loses credibility across multiple seeds—that local/global gradient pattern I saw with seed=42 disappears when I aggregate the data, which weakens the claim about operator-specific recovery effects. I can still argue for resilience over recovery, but I'll need to move the per-operator findings to the appendix since reviewers will push back on that. The statistical power is also a real constraint: with only 55-60 episodes per operator, I don't have enough signal to detect operator-level effects reliably, and even doubling the data wouldn't solve it—I'd need a substantially larger task benchmark to make that claim stick.\n\nNow I'm planning to replicate the core findings on LLaMA-3.1-8B using the same setup: three seeds across vanilla, TaxEI, and recovery conditions with identical training data and LoRA settings, to verify whether the destabilization effect generalizes across model architectures. Looking at the performance gaps, LLaMA shows a catastrophic drop of 13.5 percentage points on one seed compared to vanilla, and trails random recovery by 7.1 points overall. The cross-model analysis reveals that while both LLaMA and Qwen exhibit TaxEI instability in the same direction, the severity differs—LLaMA's standard deviation ratio of 4.1x matches the expected range, suggesting the instability pattern is consistent across models even if the magnitude varies. 结构化注入在不同架构上的失败模式不同——Qwen表现为一致的性能下降，而LLaMA则呈现灾难性的随机波动——但3个seed的样本量不足以统计上区分这些差异。LLaMA意外产生了26%的检测率（Qwen为0%），这可能反映架构差异但也混淆了跨模型比较。有趣的是，随机噪声在LLaMA上略有帮助（+3.5pp），与Qwen的结果相反，这支持了随机扰动相对无害甚至有益的假设。\n\n整体方向一致——TaxEI不稳定，Random稳定——但由于seed数量有限，这些发现只能作为两个架构上的初步证据，而不是确认的跨架构规律。论文的表述需要从\"跨架构发现\"调整为\"两个模型上的初步证据\"。\n\n现在看一下恢复率的对比数据。\n\nQwen3-8B用5个seed，LLaMA-3.1-8B用3个seed，两个模型在Vanilla、TaxEI和Random条件下的表现差异明显，特别是TaxEI的标准差差异很大（0.75×对4.1×），而且LLaMA上出现灾难性失败的比例更高。再看LLaMA的逐seed分解，不同seed之间的恢复率波动较大，尤其是s123在TaxEI条件下的表现明显下降。\n\n现在我要用配对柱状图展示这两个模型的对比，包括误差条，突出TaxEI不稳定性的方向一致但严重程度不同的特点。\n\n然后用点图显示LLaMA在种子级别的表现，特别标注那个灾难性的异常值。\n\n关键问题是LLaMA的复现结果是把双刃剑——虽然验证了跨模型的不稳定性模式，但只用3个种子太有限了，必须明确说明这只是初步证据。审稿人肯定会指出单个异常值驱动了4.1倍的标准差，以及两个模型之间26%的检测率差异。\n\n我需要承认这个限制，加入功率分析说明需要5个种子，然后解释这个差异可能反映了不同架构的学习特性——LLaMA的指令跟随能力vs Qwen的任务完成导向。关键是强调方向一致性而不是数值匹配作为跨模型证据的标准。\n\n现在看到规模消融实验，要把成功轨迹从500扩展到2500左右。\n\n我在查看预期结果，看起来TaxEI的性能差距会从-9.0缩小到-6.4，这表明数据规模不足可能是导致失败的因素。同时灾难性种子的比例会降到0，训练彩票的范围也会从19缩小到12。\n\n关键是，虽然扩大规模会缩小差距，但不会完全消除它——Vanilla从67.3%提升到71.2%，而TaxEI从58.3%提升到64.8%，这是因为embodied planning中的根本性错误模式会产生相互冲突的学习信号，这个问题不会因为数据量增加而消失。\n\nRandom也有类似的改进轨迹，但结构化的偏差比随机噪声更具持久性。更多数据确实稳定了训练过程，消除了灾难性的seed分数，但任务结构本身的影响仍然存在——这会让审稿人认为我们部分解决了数据量混淆的问题，但他们会指出2,500条轨迹相比PALADIN的50K+仍然远远不足。\n\n而且ALFWorld只有约134个独特任务，所以增加数据实际上是重复相同任务而非增加任务多样性，这削弱了scale论证的说服力。Cohen's d从1.58降至1.1，虽然仍属于大效应量，但Welch t检验仍未达到显著性（p=0.065），这是典型的中等档结果——效应减弱但方向一致，统计证据仍然不足。\n\nGenerating markdown table... Now I'm looking at how performance scales with more training data across the three conditions—the gap narrows from 9.0pp to 6.4pp when moving from 500 to 2500 trajectories, and catastrophic failures disappear entirely, suggesting data scale stabilizes training but doesn't resolve the underlying task incompatibility. Reviewers will likely push back on this interpretation, arguing either that more data could close the gap completely or that the task diversity itself is the limiting factor.\n\nThe framing should emphasize that while increasing data 5× does help, the residual gap combined with ALFWorld's ceiling of only 134 unique tasks versus PALADIN's thousands points to task-structural differences as the primary driver. Next I'm planning to test recovery prompting by providing a few in-context examples during evaluation that show error detection and correction sequences, isolating whether the model can recover from failures when given that signal without relying on training data. The few-shot improvement is consistent across all conditions because in-context examples teach the model what recovery looks like—a general capability of LLMs that doesn't depend on training. This also confirms that error injection during training didn't actually create recovery ability, since TaxEI shows the same few-shot gains as Vanilla rather than benefiting more.\n\nDetection rates jump from 0% to ~15% with examples, suggesting the model can mimic the format but struggles to execute reliably—a stark contrast to training, where even explicit error tag exposure doesn't teach detection. The modest 5pp improvement overall indicates that even with recovery templates, the cascading nature of planning errors makes recovery fundamentally difficult, which reviewers will likely see as an expected control rather than a surprising finding. 。\n这个实验的价值在于completeness而非novelty。现在看着few-shot recovery prompting的结果——所有条件下的改进幅度都差不多，ANOVA检验也显示没有显著差异，这其实是在验证一个关键点：如果TaxEI的错误意识真的来自训练时的注入，那它应该能从少样本例子中获得更大的收益才对。但结果表明训练时的错误注入对恢复能力的贡献为零，这进一步强化了resilience而非recovery的叙述。在论文中这应该作为Discussion里的简短段落出现，而不是主要结果。\n\n现在转向多种子的深度分析，用5个不同的随机种子来检验单个operator的恢复率是否稳定。之前在seed=42下看到C4有+9.1pp的提升，P1没变化，C1和P2都下降了8.3pp，现在要验证这些差异是否真实存在还是只是噪声。\n\n预期结果显示这些效应在多种子平均后会大幅衰减——C4只剩+1.8pp，P1变成-1.2pp，C1和P2分别是-3.4pp和-4.1pp，而且方差很高（C4的种子内标准差达12.5pp），Fisher精确检验对所有operator都不显著，局部-全局梯度的模式也没有复现。\n\n我认为原始发现的信号来自极小的样本量（每个operator只有11-12个任务×1个种子），单个任务的成功/失败就能驱动±9pp的效应，但当扩展到5个种子时这种信号被稀释了。P2可能保留弱负方向是因为子目标删除是最\"全局级联\"的操作——删除一个子目标会使整个后续目标链失效。\n\n相比之下，C4的观察掩蔽是最\"局部\"的操作，它在seed=42中表现好可能只是因为那个特定评估集中被掩蔽的任务恰好与TaxEI的训练分布对齐，但这种对齐在多种子聚合后被稀释了。虽然4个操作符之间的局部性排名与TaxEI优势的Spearman相关性在统计上无意义（样本太少），但方向上暗示局部操作符比全局操作符更有利，所以论文可以将其框架化为\"假设生成性\"的发现并附加适当的警告。\n\n不过审稿人会指出这实际上是在每个操作符单元约55-60个样本上进行多次统计检验，这是一个样本量不足的\"钓鱼式\"探索，应该被降级到附录中。\n\nGenerating comparison table... The per-operator analysis shows the seed-42 results don't hold up across multiple seeds—the effect sizes collapse by over 70% and all statistical tests come back non-significant. This is fine for the paper since the main claims don't depend on per-operator patterns anyway, so I'll note this in the appendix with a caveat that while the directional pattern aligns with our error cascading hypothesis, we'd need larger benchmarks to confirm per-operator effects. Now I'm looking at plans to scale up the trajectory collection from the current 501 samples.\n\nThe next phase involves expanding GPT-5.2 trajectories to around 2,500 successful ones to test whether data scale is actually the bottleneck for TaxEI's performance within ALFWorld's diversity ceiling of 134 unique tasks. I'll do this in stages—collect 1,000 first to check the trend, then decide whether to push to 2,500. The expected metrics show this would cost about $44 and yield roughly 18.7 trajectories per task on average, with the gap between vanilla and TaxEI narrowing from 9 percentage points down to around 7 as we scale up.\n\nLooking at the projected results, scaling to 2,500 trajectories generates about 22,000 clean samples—a 5× increase from the current 4,358—which improves performance across all conditions, though the TaxEI gap persists at around 6.4 percentage points. The core tension here is that reviewers will likely push back on whether we're actually adding task diversity or just collecting more trajectories for the same 134 tasks, which raises questions about whether this experiment truly addresses the fundamental limitations.\n\nThe diminishing returns pattern is clear: as we scale from 500 to 1,000 to 2,500 trajectories, the gap narrows from roughly 9 to 7 to 6.4 percentage points, suggesting we're hitting an asymptotic ceiling. This ceiling appears to be rooted in ALFWorld's inherent constraint—PALADIN's 50,000+ trajectories span thousands of unique API patterns, while our 2,500 trajectories only cover 134 unique task templates, which fundamentally limits how much scale alone can help. Training time scales proportionally at around 54 hours total across conditions and seeds, though with distributed training on 4×5090 GPUs the wall-clock time comes down to roughly 17 hours.\n\nA reviewer would likely acknowledge that scaling partially addresses the data volume confound but can't fully resolve it within ALFWorld's constraints, and would reasonably suggest that a stronger test would require a benchmark with over 1,000 unique tasks—a fair point we'd acknowledge as future work.\n\nGenerating markdown table...\n\nThe scale-up experiment serves two key purposes: it partially addresses the reviewer's concern about data volume confounding by showing the gap persists even at 5× scale, and it reveals that ALFWorld's task diversity is fundamentally limited. The core insight is that the gap remains even as we increase training data, pointing to the underlying diversity ceiling. 从9.0→6.4pp（29% reduction）but not eliminated，且diminishing returns curve suggests even 10× more data wouldn't close it。This is the strongest argument for task-structure over data-scale explanation——但only if properly framed with the diversity ceiling caveat。\n\nPaper应include the 3-point scale curve (500/1000/2500) to visually demonstrate diminishing returns，并annotate PALADIN's 50K+ scale at the far right to show the magnitude of the gap。Text should say: \"Even at 5× training scale, the injection penalty persists (-6.4pp), and the diminishing-returns curve suggests the residual gap is driven by task-structural factors rather than data volume. However, we cannot fully rule out scale effects without matching PALADIN's training volume, which is infeasible within ALFWorld's task diversity ceiling.\"\n\nNow I'm pulling the actual recovery eval results from the registry to verify my predictions against the real data—checking the vanilla and TaxEI recovery rates across all seeds to see if they match what I expected. The recovery rates all fall within the acceptable range compared to clean rates. Since the actual LLaMA data already exists and aligns well with the median tier parameters—the standard deviation ratio of 4.1 fits within the expected [3.5, 4.5] range and the catastrophic fraction of ~0.33 matches the upper bound—I can use that actual data to finalize the predictions.\n\nGenerating YAML output...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_read_input_tokens":53604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30ce2e14-84d3-47ec-abae-17f1dfd2f6a2","uuid":"19a1d61b-d261-4b07-9548-67059f7fce5b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KjDCXjCEfoHAJvqjWeT8DL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"找到 experiment_plan，提取所有 status: planned 的实验并生成 median 档预测。\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims systematic降级：(1)'Cross-architecture generalization'→'preliminary cross-model evidence on two architectures'；\n  (2)主finding→'large effect size suggestive of harm, requiring larger N for confirmation'；\n  (3)增加prominent limitations section：power=45% at n=5, Bonferroni NS；\n  (4)structured-vs-random divergence从'proves'→'suggests'；\n  (5)补充2×2 meta-analysis框架(PALADIN+EEF+TaxEI: {positive/negative signal}×{tool-use/planning})提升conceptual novelty；\n  (6)加入explicit power curve showing n=9 threshold for 80% power。\n  Reviewer mean score 2.8–3.2 (Borderline Accept)。论文可发EMNLP Findings但tone从\n  'definitive boundary condition'变为'empirical evidence toward boundary conditions'。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Eval Multi-Seed (5-seed × 3 conditions)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-eval-multiseed\"\n    description: >\n      将recovery eval从seed=42扩展至全部5个seed (42/0/123/1/7)，覆盖V/T/R三条件。\n      每条件47 tasks × 4 operators (P1/P2/C1/C4) round-robin注入。验证D041\n      resilience-not-recovery发现的跨seed稳定性。~15 GPU-h，需先retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 67.1\n      vanilla_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 4.9\n      vanilla_recovery_per_seed: [61.7, 68.1, 66.0, 66.0, 74.5]\n      taxei_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 57.4\n      taxei_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 6.2\n      taxei_recovery_per_seed: [59.6, 46.8, 61.7, 61.7, 57.4]\n      random_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 57.9\n      random_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 6.4\n      random_recovery_per_seed: [63.8, 55.3, 66.0, 51.1, 53.2]\n      recovery_minus_clean_vanilla_pp: -0.2\n      recovery_minus_clean_taxei_pp: -0.9\n      recovery_minus_clean_random_pp: -0.4\n      detection_rate_qwen_all_seeds: 0.0\n      welch_t_taxei_vs_vanilla_recovery_p: 0.030\n      welch_t_bonferroni_significant: false\n      cohens_d_recovery_taxei_vs_vanilla: 1.53\n      per_operator_C4_5seed_taxei_advantage_pp: 1.8\n      per_operator_C4_fisher_p: 0.71\n      per_operator_P2_5seed_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -4.1\n      per_operator_P2_fisher_p: 0.38\n      per_operator_local_global_gradient_replicates: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档核心参数recovery_clean_rate_match_pp=[0.0, 2.0]。5-seed recovery eval\n      确认D041的resilience-not-recovery pattern：每条件recovery rate与clean eval rate\n      偏差<1pp（V: 67.1 vs 67.3=-0.2pp; T: 57.4 vs 58.3=-0.9pp; R: 57.9 vs 58.3=-0.4pp）。\n      模型通过任务完成能力被动忽略eval-time perturbation而非主动检测修正——\n      recovery rate本质上就是clean task completion rate在noisy evaluation下的表现。\n      Detection rate维持0%（Qwen架构在任何seed/条件下都不产生显式error flagging）。\n\n      Per-operator patterns是关键降级点：seed=42中C4+9.1pp的\"优势\"基于N=11单个task\n      flip(6→7/11)，5-seed聚合后collapse至+1.8pp(Fisher p=0.71 NS)。P2保持weak\n      negative direction(-4.1pp)但同样NS。整个local/global gradient从confirmatory\n      降级为\"directional observation consistent with error cascading hypothesis,\n      requiring >200-task benchmarks for per-operator claims\"。\n\n      这个实验的统计结构：5 seeds × 47 tasks = 235 episodes/condition for aggregate\n      recovery claim (adequate power for ~10pp effect)，但per-operator仅~55-60 episodes\n      (grossly underpowered for ~5pp operator-level effects)。Median档reviewer会accept\n      aggregate resilience finding但要求per-operator移至Appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Seed Recovery vs Clean Rate Match\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | Clean 5s Mean±SD | Recovery 5s Mean±SD | Δ(Rec−Clean) | Det. Rate |\n          |-----------|:----------------:|:-------------------:|:------------:|:---------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 67.3 ± 4.7      | 67.1 ± 4.9         | −0.2pp       | 0%        |\n          | TaxEI     | 58.3 ± 6.5      | 57.4 ± 6.2         | −0.9pp       | 0%        |\n          | Random    | 58.3 ± 8.7      | 57.9 ± 6.4         | −0.4pp       | 0%        |\n      - name: \"Per-Operator TaxEI−Vanilla Δ: Seed=42 vs 5-Seed\"\n        content: |\n          | Operator            | Locality | Seed=42 Δ | 5s Mean Δ | 5s SD   | Fisher p |\n          |---------------------|:--------:|:---------:|:---------:|:-------:|:--------:|\n          | C4_obs_masking      | Local    | +9.1pp    | +1.8pp    | 12.5pp  | 0.71     |\n          | P1_step_order_swap  | Mixed    |  0.0pp    | −1.2pp    | 10.8pp  | 0.82     |\n          | C1_context_trunc    | Global   | −8.3pp    | −3.4pp    | 11.2pp  | 0.49     |\n          | P2_subgoal_deletion | Global   | −8.3pp    | −4.1pp    | 13.1pp  | 0.38     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Recovery Rate vs Clean Eval Rate scatter (15 points = 5 seeds × 3 conditions)，\n         y=x reference line。Points cluster within ±2pp of diagonal，visually confirming\n         resilience-not-recovery。V=blue, T=red, R=orange。\"\n      - \"Per-operator dot plot：4 operators × 5 seeds的TaxEI−Vanilla Δ，large scatter\n         覆盖zero line，seed=42 highlighted as outlier-driven。\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-seed recovery eval的aggregate finding（recovery≈clean rate）是paper的strongest\n      confirmatory result——不依赖p-value而是qualitative pattern match。但per-operator\n      gradient从Results正文降级至Appendix。Reviewer会accept \"resilience not recovery\"\n      作为valid finding但不accept per-operator作为stand-alone claim。This experiment\n      changes paper structure: Table 3 (per-operator) moves to Appendix B, replaced by\n      a compact \"recovery≈clean\" comparison table in main text.\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Cross-Model Replication (3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"llama-cross-model\"\n    description: >\n      在LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct上复制核心实验：3 seeds (42/0/123) × 3条件 (V/T/R)。\n      同训练数据、LoRA配置(rank=16, α=32)、eval protocol。验证TaxEI instability\n      是否跨architecture成立。~36 GPU-h。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_mean: 73.1\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_sd: 2.5\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 74.5, 70.2]\n      llama_taxei_recovery_mean: 69.5\n      llama_taxei_recovery_sd: 8.6\n      llama_taxei_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 74.5, 59.6]\n      llama_random_recovery_mean: 76.6\n      llama_random_recovery_sd: 2.1\n      llama_random_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 76.6, 78.7]\n      llama_vanilla_clean_mean: 72.3\n      llama_vanilla_clean_sd: 0.0\n      llama_taxei_clean_mean: 71.6\n      llama_taxei_clean_sd: 8.6\n      llama_random_clean_mean: 75.9\n      llama_random_clean_sd: 1.2\n      taxei_sd_over_random_sd: 4.1\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.33\n      catastrophic_seed_id: s123\n      catastrophic_drop_vs_vanilla_pp: -10.6\n      catastrophic_drop_vs_random_pp: -19.1\n      taxei_mean_vs_random_mean_pp: -7.1\n      taxei_mean_vs_vanilla_mean_pp: -3.6\n      llama_detection_rate_mean: 0.27\n      cross_model_direction_consistent: true\n      welch_t_taxei_vs_vanilla_llama_p: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档cross_model_taxei_sd_ratio=[3.5, 4.5]，catastrophic_seed_fraction=[0.2, 0.33]。\n\n      TaxEI SD=8.6pp vs Random SD=2.1pp → ratio=4.1×，落在区间中间。这个ratio由\n      single catastrophic seed(s123)驱动：s123 recovery=59.6%（vs vanilla 70.2%=-10.6pp，\n      vs random 78.7%=-19.1pp），而s42/s0均=74.5%（与vanilla持平）。Pattern mirrors Qwen\n      的catastrophic seed现象但表现形式不同：Qwen是consistent degradation（所有5个seed\n      都低于vanilla），LLaMA是intermittent catastrophe（2/3 neutral, 1/3 catastrophic）。\n\n      Reviewer challenge点：(1)\"n=3的SD estimate有极宽CI——单个outlier就能创造4× ratio\"。\n      这是valid的——remove s123后TaxEI SD=0pp。但counter-argument是catastrophic seed\n      本身就是structured injection的核心failure mode。(2)\"LLaMA detection rate 27%\n      vs Qwen 0%——不同architecture在学不同的东西，cross-model comparison的前提被undermined。\"\n      这需要在paper中讨论为architecture-dependent behavior。(3)\"3 seeds on second model\n      is preliminary at best。1/3=33% catastrophic could be 0/10 with more seeds。\"\n\n      Random在LLaMA上mildly beneficial(76.6%>vanilla 73.1%,+3.5pp)——与Qwen(Random=\n      Vanilla degraded)形成对比。这支持\"unstructured noise is benign-to-helpful\"但也\n      表明effect magnitude是model-dependent。Paper必须从\"cross-architecture confirmation\"\n      降级为\"preliminary evidence on two architectures suggesting direction consistency\"。\n\n      Detection rate差异（LLaMA ~27% vs Qwen 0%）是unexpected finding。LLaMA-3.1的\n      instruction-following tendency更强，可能使其more likely to verbalize error awareness\n      即使这种awareness doesn't translate to improved recovery。这实际上strengthens\n      \"detection ≠ recovery\"的argument但需要careful framing。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Model Recovery Rate Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          |              | Qwen3-8B (5-seed)  | LLaMA-3.1-8B (3-seed) |\n          |--------------|:------------------:|:---------------------:|\n          | Vanilla      | 67.3 ± 4.7        | 73.1 ± 2.5           |\n          | TaxEI        | 58.3 ± 6.5        | 69.5 ± 8.6           |\n          | Random       | 58.3 ± 8.7        | 76.6 ± 2.1           |\n          | V−T gap      | −9.0pp             | −3.6pp                |\n          | T SD / R SD  | 0.75×              | 4.1×                  |\n          | Catastrophic | 1/5 (20%)          | 1/3 (33%)             |\n          | Detection    | 0%                 | 27%                   |\n      - name: \"LLaMA Per-Seed Recovery Breakdown\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition       | s42   | s0    | s123       | Mean ± SD     |\n          |-----------------|:-----:|:-----:|:----------:|:-------------:|\n          | Vanilla (rec.)  | 74.5  | 74.5  | 70.2       | 73.1 ± 2.5   |\n          | TaxEI (rec.)    | 74.5  | 74.5  | **59.6**   | 69.5 ± 8.6   |\n          | Random (rec.)   | 74.5  | 76.6  | 78.7       | 76.6 ± 2.1   |\n          | Vanilla (clean) | 72.3  | 72.3  | 72.3       | 72.3 ± 0.0   |\n          | TaxEI (clean)   | 76.6  | 76.6  | **61.7**   | 71.6 ± 8.6   |\n          | Random (clean)  | 74.5  | 76.6  | 76.6       | 75.9 ± 1.2   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart：Qwen 5-seed vs LLaMA 3-seed，V/T/R with error bars。\n         Direction一致（TaxEI最不稳定）但severity profile不同。\"\n      - \"Seed-level dot plot for LLaMA：TaxEI s123 catastrophic outlier突出，\n         Random三点紧密聚集。Annotated with catastrophic threshold line。\"\n      - \"Detection rate comparison bar：Qwen 0% vs LLaMA 27%，分operator。\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA replication是median档的关键升级——将finding从\"single-model negative result\"\n      升级为\"cross-model evidence\"——但3-seed limitation使其只能是preliminary。\n      Direction consistency（TaxEI unstable across both models）是可claim的；\n      magnitude consistency不可claim（Qwen consistent -9pp vs LLaMA intermittent -3.6pp）。\n\n      最大reviewer risk是detection rate差异：如果LLaMA produces 27% detection而Qwen 0%，\n      reviewer会argue the models learn fundamentally different representations from same data，\n      undermining \"cross-model\" claim的validity。Counter：detection doesn't improve recovery\n      (LLaMA TaxEI detection 30% but recovery 69.5% ≈ vanilla 73.1%)，so detection is\n      orthogonal to the stability finding。\n\n      Paper claim wording必须是：\"Structured error injection destabilizes training on\n      both Qwen3-8B (consistent harm, 5-seed) and LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct (intermittent\n      catastrophic failure, 3-seed preliminary), while random injection remains stable\n      across both architectures.\"\n\n  - name: \"Scale Ablation (25K–50K trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-ablation\"\n    description: >\n      将训练数据从~500成功轨迹(4,358 clean samples)扩展至~2,500轨迹(~22K clean samples)，\n      训练V/T/R三条件(3-seed each)。测试TaxEI failure是否primarily due to data scale。\n      ~$44 API + ~54 GPU-h (3-seed×3 conditions with DDP)。\n    expected_results:\n      scaled_vanilla_mean: 71.2\n      scaled_vanilla_sd: 3.5\n      scaled_taxei_mean: 64.8\n      scaled_taxei_sd: 5.2\n      scaled_random_mean: 66.3\n      scaled_random_sd: 4.1\n      gap_taxei_vs_vanilla_pp: -6.4\n      gap_random_vs_vanilla_pp: -4.9\n      gap_taxei_vs_random_pp: -1.5\n      gap_reduction_pct_from_baseline: 29\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.0\n      training_lottery_range_pp: 12.0\n      cohens_d_scaled: 1.05\n      welch_t_scaled_p: 0.065\n      welch_t_bonferroni_significant: false\n      collection_cost_usd: 44.0\n      unique_tasks_covered: 134\n      trajectories_per_task: 18.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档预测scale-up narrows gap但不eliminate。核心逻辑：\n\n      (1) Vanilla受益最稳定(67.3→71.2%,+3.9pp)：更多clean data直接improve task completion，\n      无conflicting signals。接近ALFWorld的performance ceiling (~75-80% for 8B models)。\n\n      (2) TaxEI gap从-9.0pp缩小至-6.4pp(reduction 29%)：更多data提供更robust的clean\n      signal base，partially buffering against injection noise。但fundamental conflict\n      (structured error patterns vs clean trajectories创造contradictory gradients)不因\n      data volume消失——P2_SubGoalDeletion在任何scale下都会teach \"skip steps is OK\"\n      然后clean data teach \"don't skip steps\"。\n\n      (3) Random gap缩小更多(-9.0→-4.9pp, reduction 46%)：random noise at scale\n      tends to average out(law of large numbers)，而structured patterns maintain\n      systematic bias。这一差异支持\"structured > random for harm\"的claim。\n\n      (4) Catastrophic seed fraction降至0%：5× more data stabilize training dynamics，\n      eliminating the bimodal seed distribution。Training lottery range从19-23pp降至~12pp。\n      这是data scale的genuine positive effect——与\"task structure causes the gap\"不矛盾，\n      因为stability和mean performance是可分离的维度。\n\n      (5) Cohen's d从1.58降至1.05(仍large但approaching medium)，Welch t=0.065(NS)。\n      在median档这意味着：effect real but smaller at scale, still insufficient stat power。\n\n      (6) ALFWorld diversity ceiling：2,500 trajectories ÷ 134 unique tasks = ~19 repetitions/task。\n      PALADIN trains on thousands of unique API patterns。Our \"scale-up\" is actually\n      \"repetition-up\"——Reviewer会correctly identify这个distinction。\n\n      Reviewer典型response：\"The gap narrows 29% at 5× scale, suggesting data volume IS\n      a contributing factor. You cannot claim task structure is the 'primary' cause without\n      matching PALADIN's diversity.\" Median档paper降级claim为：\"Data scale contributes to\n      the failure (29% gap reduction at 5×) but does not fully account for it. The residual\n      6.4pp gap, combined with ALFWorld's 134-task diversity ceiling, points to\n      task-structural differences as a co-dominant factor.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Scale Ablation: 500 vs 2500 Trajectories\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | 500-traj (5s) | 2500-traj (3s) | Δ     | Gap vs V |\n          |-----------|:------------:|:--------------:|:-----:|:--------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 67.3 ± 4.7  | 71.2 ± 3.5    | +3.9  | —        |\n          | TaxEI     | 58.3 ± 6.5  | 64.8 ± 5.2    | +6.5  | −6.4pp   |\n          | Random    | 58.3 ± 8.7  | 66.3 ± 4.1    | +8.0  | −4.9pp   |\n          | Cohen's d | 1.58         | 1.05           | −0.53 | —        |\n          | Catast. % | 20%          | 0%             | elim. | —        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Performance vs log(training_samples) curve for V/T/R。Diminishing returns明显，\n         persistent gap可视化。X轴annotate PALADIN 50K+位置(far right, extrapolated)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale ablation在median档是partial mitigation。Gap减少29%但persist——足以让reviewer\n      同时argue \"scale matters\" AND \"structure matters\"。Paper需要honest framing：\n      \"Increasing data 5× narrows the penalty from 9pp to 6.4pp and eliminates catastrophic\n      seeds, indicating data volume is a contributing factor. The residual gap and\n      ALFWorld's diversity ceiling suggest task structure as a co-dominant factor.\"\n      这是比\"task structure is the primary factor\"弱的claim，但对median档reviewer可接受。\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Prompting (Few-Shot In-Context)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-prompting\"\n    description: >\n      Eval时为每个condition提供2/4个in-context recovery examples（展示error→detection→\n      correction序列），测试few-shot能否isolate recovery knowledge vs training signal。\n      如果V/T/R equally benefit，说明recovery能力来自ICL而非SFT。Seed=42, 47 tasks。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_0shot_recovery: 61.7\n      vanilla_2shot_recovery: 65.3\n      vanilla_4shot_recovery: 68.1\n      taxei_0shot_recovery: 59.6\n      taxei_2shot_recovery: 63.2\n      taxei_4shot_recovery: 66.0\n      random_0shot_recovery: 63.8\n      random_4shot_recovery: 68.1\n      improvement_vanilla_4shot_pp: 6.4\n      improvement_taxei_4shot_pp: 6.4\n      improvement_random_4shot_pp: 4.3\n      between_condition_4shot_anova_p: 0.78\n      detection_rate_4shot: 0.15\n      detection_rate_0shot: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档预测few-shot prompting universally提升所有条件，无条件间差异。\n\n      (1) ICL provides \"what recovery looks like\" template——是LLM的general能力，\n      与SFT training regime无关。V/T/R同等受益(+4-6pp)证明SFT期间的error injection\n      没有创造任何可被ICL amplify的recovery capability。若TaxEI训练真的teach了latent\n      recovery ability，应该看到TaxEI从few-shot中disproportionately benefit（additive\n      effect: SFT recovery knowledge + ICL recovery template = super-additive）。\n      实际结果：TaxEI improvement = Vanilla improvement = ~6.4pp → zero SFT contribution。\n\n      (2) Detection rate从0%→~15%：ICL examples provide detection template，LLM能\n      模仿format但不reliable执行。这与SFT 0% detection对比：即使explicit error tag\n      exposure during SFT不teach detection，但4个in-context examples partially do。\n      暗示SFT signal在fine-tuning过程中被downstream pattern corruption覆盖，而ICL\n      operates at a more superficial level that preserves detection formatting。\n\n      (3) 4-shot improvement ~5pp mean modest——远低于closing gap to vanilla clean(67.3%)。\n      Even with explicit recovery templates，embodied planning的cascading error nature\n      使genuine recovery fundamentally hard。Models can detect ~15% of errors and still\n      fail to recover from most of them。\n\n      (4) Reviewer视为\"expected given resilience finding\"——如果D041已confirmed\n      resilience-not-recovery，few-shot control是belt-and-suspenders。Value在于\n      completeness而非novelty。Paper中应放Discussion短段而非main result。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Few-Shot Recovery Prompting (seed=42)\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | 0-shot | 2-shot | 4-shot | Δ(4s−0s) | Det.(4s) |\n          |-----------|:------:|:------:|:------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 61.7%  | 65.3%  | 68.1%  | +6.4pp   | 14.9%    |\n          | TaxEI     | 59.6%  | 63.2%  | 66.0%  | +6.4pp   | 14.9%    |\n          | Random    | 63.8%  | 66.0%  | 68.1%  | +4.3pp   | 17.0%    |\n          | ANOVA     | —      | —      | F=0.26, p=0.78 | —  | —        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: shots (0/2/4) × 3 conditions。三条线near-parallel上升，\n         证明improvement is additive-from-ICL而非condition-dependent。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Recovery prompting是clean control but在median档不改变paper narrative。\n      它confirms D041 from a different angle。Paper allocation：Discussion section\n      1段，\"In-context recovery examples provide comparable improvement across all\n      conditions (ANOVA NS), confirming that error injection training does not create\n      latent recovery capacity that can be unlocked by prompting.\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-Operator Deep Dive (Multi-Seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-operator-deepdive\"\n    description: >\n      利用recovery-eval-multiseed的5-seed数据，对4个operator分别计算multi-seed\n      TaxEI−Vanilla recovery delta。验证seed=42的local/global gradient是否replicate。\n    expected_results:\n      C4_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: 1.8\n      C4_5seed_sd_pp: 12.5\n      C4_fisher_p: 0.71\n      P1_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -1.2\n      P1_5seed_sd_pp: 10.8\n      P1_fisher_p: 0.82\n      C1_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -3.4\n      C1_5seed_sd_pp: 11.2\n      C1_fisher_p: 0.49\n      P2_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -4.1\n      P2_5seed_sd_pp: 13.1\n      P2_fisher_p: 0.38\n      local_global_gradient_direction_preserved: true\n      local_global_gradient_magnitude_collapsed: true\n      spearman_locality_rank_vs_advantage: 0.60\n      spearman_p: 0.42\n      episodes_per_operator_cell: 57\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档per-operator gradient在multi-seed后collapse to noise。\n\n      (1) Seed=42的C4=+9.1pp基于11个episodes中1个flip(6→7)——本质上是coin flip。\n      5-seed聚合后~57 episodes/operator/condition给每个operator ~±8-13pp的SD。\n      C4的mean从+9.1→+1.8pp，Fisher p=0.71——signal消失在variance中。\n\n      (2) Direction weakly preserved：local operators(C4)仍slightly positive(+1.8pp)，\n      global operators(C1,P2)仍negative(−3.4, −4.1pp)。但magnitude减小~70%，且\n      Spearman rank correlation(n=4)完全uninformative(p=0.42)。\n\n      (3) P2(sub_goal_deletion)保持最negative(−4.1pp)——合理因为sub-goal deletion是\n      most globally cascading的operator。但Fisher p=0.38 NS，无法distinguish from noise。\n\n      (4) 这个实验的value是将per-operator analysis从\"interesting pattern\"降级为\n      \"hypothesis for future work with larger benchmarks\"。Reviewer会agree这个降级。\n      Paper中从Results Table移至Appendix exploratory analysis。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Operator Recovery Analysis (5-seed)\"\n        content: |\n          | Operator      | Locality | s42 Δ  | 5s Mean Δ | 5s SD   | Fisher p | N/cell |\n          |---------------|:--------:|:------:|:---------:|:-------:|:--------:|:------:|\n          | C4_obs_mask   | Local    | +9.1pp | +1.8pp    | 12.5pp  | 0.71     | ~57    |\n          | P1_step_swap  | Mixed    |  0.0pp | −1.2pp    | 10.8pp  | 0.82     | ~57    |\n          | C1_ctx_trunc  | Global   | −8.3pp | −3.4pp    | 11.2pp  | 0.49     | ~57    |\n          | P2_subgoal_del| Global   | −8.3pp | −4.1pp    | 13.1pp  | 0.38     | ~57    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strip plot：每operator每seed一个点(20 points total)，massive scatter，\n         zero line贯穿所有operators。Seed=42用红色标记为outlier-driven。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-operator deep dive confirms this analysis is exploratory-only。对paper的impact\n      minimal——main claims不依赖per-operator patterns。Appendix B一页足够。关键句：\n      \"While the directional pattern (local operators neutral, global operators harmful)\n      is consistent with our error cascading hypothesis, per-operator effects are not\n      statistically distinguishable from noise at N≈57 per cell. Benchmarks with >200\n      diverse tasks are needed for per-operator claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"Scale-Up Data Collection (500→2500 Trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-up-data\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-5.2 trajectory collection从501扩展至~2,500成功轨迹。分阶段：先1,000 check\n      trend再决定2,500。ALFWorld diversity ceiling ~134 unique tasks。~$44 API cost。\n    expected_results:\n      phase1_1000_trajectories: 1000\n      phase1_1000_cost_usd: 17.6\n      phase1_1000_success_rate: 0.70\n      phase1_1000_unique_tasks: 134\n      phase1_1000_traj_per_task: 7.5\n      phase1_1000_taxei_gap_trend_pp: -7.1\n      phase2_2500_trajectories: 2500\n      phase2_2500_cost_usd: 44.0\n      phase2_2500_traj_per_task: 18.7\n      phase2_2500_samples_clean: 21790\n      phase2_2500_samples_injected: 18400\n      phase2_total_training_time_h: 54\n      phase2_wall_clock_ddp_h: 17\n      diminishing_returns_500_to_1000_gap_reduction_pp: 1.9\n      diminishing_returns_1000_to_2500_gap_reduction_pp: 0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scale-up data collection在median档是feasibility + diminishing returns story。\n\n      (1) Collection feasibility confirmed：70% success rate stable（与initial 501-traj\n      collection一致），cost linear($8.86/500≈$44/2500)。无technical barrier。\n\n      (2) Phase 1 (1,000-traj) gap已经narrow(9.0→7.1pp)，phase 2 (2,500) further\n      narrow(7.1→6.4pp)——clear diminishing returns。500→1000 gains 1.9pp，\n      1000→2500 only 0.7pp。Extrapolating logarithmically，5000 traj would yield\n      ~5.5pp gap——仍non-zero。\n\n      (3) ALFWorld diversity ceiling是fundamental：134 unique tasks × 18.7 repetitions\n      = pure repetition augmentation。PALADIN's advantage可能是task diversity\n      (thousands of unique API call patterns)而非volume。Paper应explicit state：\n      \"Within ALFWorld's 134-task diversity ceiling, data scale reduction accounts for\n      ~29% of the injection penalty. The remaining gap likely reflects task-structural\n      differences that cannot be resolved by repetition-based scaling.\"\n\n      (4) 训练resource significant(54 GPU-h total for 3s×3c)但feasible with 4×5090。\n      Question is ROI：这个experiment对reviewer的说服力是moderate——它addresses\n      concern #10 partially but opens the door for \"you need to scale to 50K\" counter-argument。\n\n      (5) Median档reviewer response：将scale-up result视为evidence for mixed causation\n      (both scale and structure contribute)而非clean separation。这是reasonable——我们\n      不能fully disentangle scale from structure within a single benchmark。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Data Collection Scaling Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Phase | Traj | Unique Tasks | Traj/Task | Cost  | TaxEI−V Gap | Δ from prev |\n          |-------|:----:|:------------:|:---------:|:-----:|:-----------:|:-----------:|\n          | Base  | 500  | 134          | 3.7       | $8.86 | −9.0pp      | —           |\n          | Ph. 1 | 1000 | 134          | 7.5       | $17.6 | −7.1pp      | +1.9pp      |\n          | Ph. 2 | 2500 | 134          | 18.7      | $44.0 | −6.4pp      | +0.7pp      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diminishing returns curve: x=log(trajectories), y=TaxEI−Vanilla gap (pp)。\n         3 data points + logarithmic fit extrapolation to 5K/10K/50K。\n         Annotated PALADIN scale marker at 50K showing gap still projected >0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale-up data是scale-ablation的prerequisite，结果一致。Diminishing returns\n      是key visual——logarithmic fit shows gap never reaches zero within any feasible\n      ALFWorld scale。This supports task-structure argument but must be presented as\n      \"suggestive projection\" not \"proof\"。\n\n      Paper allocation：Results section一段 + diminishing returns figure。Limitation\n      section承认\"We cannot fully disentangle data scale from task structure within a\n      single benchmark. Cross-benchmark validation (e.g., ToolBench replication of TaxEI)\n      would provide stronger evidence but requires substantial engineering effort.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_read_input_tokens":53604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"30ce2e14-84d3-47ec-abae-17f1dfd2f6a2","uuid":"a88064b3-1ca6-4635-b1dc-14b3484fd09b"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":481539,"duration_api_ms":483470,"num_turns":5,"result":"找到 experiment_plan，提取所有 status: planned 的实验并生成 median 档预测。\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Claims systematic降级：(1)'Cross-architecture generalization'→'preliminary cross-model evidence on two architectures'；\n  (2)主finding→'large effect size suggestive of harm, requiring larger N for confirmation'；\n  (3)增加prominent limitations section：power=45% at n=5, Bonferroni NS；\n  (4)structured-vs-random divergence从'proves'→'suggests'；\n  (5)补充2×2 meta-analysis框架(PALADIN+EEF+TaxEI: {positive/negative signal}×{tool-use/planning})提升conceptual novelty；\n  (6)加入explicit power curve showing n=9 threshold for 80% power。\n  Reviewer mean score 2.8–3.2 (Borderline Accept)。论文可发EMNLP Findings但tone从\n  'definitive boundary condition'变为'empirical evidence toward boundary conditions'。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Eval Multi-Seed (5-seed × 3 conditions)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-eval-multiseed\"\n    description: >\n      将recovery eval从seed=42扩展至全部5个seed (42/0/123/1/7)，覆盖V/T/R三条件。\n      每条件47 tasks × 4 operators (P1/P2/C1/C4) round-robin注入。验证D041\n      resilience-not-recovery发现的跨seed稳定性。~15 GPU-h，需先retrain seed=0/123 checkpoints。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 67.1\n      vanilla_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 4.9\n      vanilla_recovery_per_seed: [61.7, 68.1, 66.0, 66.0, 74.5]\n      taxei_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 57.4\n      taxei_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 6.2\n      taxei_recovery_per_seed: [59.6, 46.8, 61.7, 61.7, 57.4]\n      random_recovery_5seed_mean_pct: 57.9\n      random_recovery_5seed_sd_pp: 6.4\n      random_recovery_per_seed: [63.8, 55.3, 66.0, 51.1, 53.2]\n      recovery_minus_clean_vanilla_pp: -0.2\n      recovery_minus_clean_taxei_pp: -0.9\n      recovery_minus_clean_random_pp: -0.4\n      detection_rate_qwen_all_seeds: 0.0\n      welch_t_taxei_vs_vanilla_recovery_p: 0.030\n      welch_t_bonferroni_significant: false\n      cohens_d_recovery_taxei_vs_vanilla: 1.53\n      per_operator_C4_5seed_taxei_advantage_pp: 1.8\n      per_operator_C4_fisher_p: 0.71\n      per_operator_P2_5seed_taxei_disadvantage_pp: -4.1\n      per_operator_P2_fisher_p: 0.38\n      per_operator_local_global_gradient_replicates: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档核心参数recovery_clean_rate_match_pp=[0.0, 2.0]。5-seed recovery eval\n      确认D041的resilience-not-recovery pattern：每条件recovery rate与clean eval rate\n      偏差<1pp（V: 67.1 vs 67.3=-0.2pp; T: 57.4 vs 58.3=-0.9pp; R: 57.9 vs 58.3=-0.4pp）。\n      模型通过任务完成能力被动忽略eval-time perturbation而非主动检测修正——\n      recovery rate本质上就是clean task completion rate在noisy evaluation下的表现。\n      Detection rate维持0%（Qwen架构在任何seed/条件下都不产生显式error flagging）。\n\n      Per-operator patterns是关键降级点：seed=42中C4+9.1pp的\"优势\"基于N=11单个task\n      flip(6→7/11)，5-seed聚合后collapse至+1.8pp(Fisher p=0.71 NS)。P2保持weak\n      negative direction(-4.1pp)但同样NS。整个local/global gradient从confirmatory\n      降级为\"directional observation consistent with error cascading hypothesis,\n      requiring >200-task benchmarks for per-operator claims\"。\n\n      这个实验的统计结构：5 seeds × 47 tasks = 235 episodes/condition for aggregate\n      recovery claim (adequate power for ~10pp effect)，但per-operator仅~55-60 episodes\n      (grossly underpowered for ~5pp operator-level effects)。Median档reviewer会accept\n      aggregate resilience finding但要求per-operator移至Appendix。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Seed Recovery vs Clean Rate Match\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | Clean 5s Mean±SD | Recovery 5s Mean±SD | Δ(Rec−Clean) | Det. Rate |\n          |-----------|:----------------:|:-------------------:|:------------:|:---------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 67.3 ± 4.7      | 67.1 ± 4.9         | −0.2pp       | 0%        |\n          | TaxEI     | 58.3 ± 6.5      | 57.4 ± 6.2         | −0.9pp       | 0%        |\n          | Random    | 58.3 ± 8.7      | 57.9 ± 6.4         | −0.4pp       | 0%        |\n      - name: \"Per-Operator TaxEI−Vanilla Δ: Seed=42 vs 5-Seed\"\n        content: |\n          | Operator            | Locality | Seed=42 Δ | 5s Mean Δ | 5s SD   | Fisher p |\n          |---------------------|:--------:|:---------:|:---------:|:-------:|:--------:|\n          | C4_obs_masking      | Local    | +9.1pp    | +1.8pp    | 12.5pp  | 0.71     |\n          | P1_step_order_swap  | Mixed    |  0.0pp    | −1.2pp    | 10.8pp  | 0.82     |\n          | C1_context_trunc    | Global   | −8.3pp    | −3.4pp    | 11.2pp  | 0.49     |\n          | P2_subgoal_deletion | Global   | −8.3pp    | −4.1pp    | 13.1pp  | 0.38     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Recovery Rate vs Clean Eval Rate scatter (15 points = 5 seeds × 3 conditions)，\n         y=x reference line。Points cluster within ±2pp of diagonal，visually confirming\n         resilience-not-recovery。V=blue, T=red, R=orange。\"\n      - \"Per-operator dot plot：4 operators × 5 seeds的TaxEI−Vanilla Δ，large scatter\n         覆盖zero line，seed=42 highlighted as outlier-driven。\"\n    analysis: >\n      5-seed recovery eval的aggregate finding（recovery≈clean rate）是paper的strongest\n      confirmatory result——不依赖p-value而是qualitative pattern match。但per-operator\n      gradient从Results正文降级至Appendix。Reviewer会accept \"resilience not recovery\"\n      作为valid finding但不accept per-operator作为stand-alone claim。This experiment\n      changes paper structure: Table 3 (per-operator) moves to Appendix B, replaced by\n      a compact \"recovery≈clean\" comparison table in main text.\n\n  - name: \"LLaMA-3.1-8B Cross-Model Replication (3-seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"llama-cross-model\"\n    description: >\n      在LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct上复制核心实验：3 seeds (42/0/123) × 3条件 (V/T/R)。\n      同训练数据、LoRA配置(rank=16, α=32)、eval protocol。验证TaxEI instability\n      是否跨architecture成立。~36 GPU-h。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_mean: 73.1\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_sd: 2.5\n      llama_vanilla_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 74.5, 70.2]\n      llama_taxei_recovery_mean: 69.5\n      llama_taxei_recovery_sd: 8.6\n      llama_taxei_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 74.5, 59.6]\n      llama_random_recovery_mean: 76.6\n      llama_random_recovery_sd: 2.1\n      llama_random_recovery_seeds: [74.5, 76.6, 78.7]\n      llama_vanilla_clean_mean: 72.3\n      llama_vanilla_clean_sd: 0.0\n      llama_taxei_clean_mean: 71.6\n      llama_taxei_clean_sd: 8.6\n      llama_random_clean_mean: 75.9\n      llama_random_clean_sd: 1.2\n      taxei_sd_over_random_sd: 4.1\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.33\n      catastrophic_seed_id: s123\n      catastrophic_drop_vs_vanilla_pp: -10.6\n      catastrophic_drop_vs_random_pp: -19.1\n      taxei_mean_vs_random_mean_pp: -7.1\n      taxei_mean_vs_vanilla_mean_pp: -3.6\n      llama_detection_rate_mean: 0.27\n      cross_model_direction_consistent: true\n      welch_t_taxei_vs_vanilla_llama_p: 0.52\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档cross_model_taxei_sd_ratio=[3.5, 4.5]，catastrophic_seed_fraction=[0.2, 0.33]。\n\n      TaxEI SD=8.6pp vs Random SD=2.1pp → ratio=4.1×，落在区间中间。这个ratio由\n      single catastrophic seed(s123)驱动：s123 recovery=59.6%（vs vanilla 70.2%=-10.6pp，\n      vs random 78.7%=-19.1pp），而s42/s0均=74.5%（与vanilla持平）。Pattern mirrors Qwen\n      的catastrophic seed现象但表现形式不同：Qwen是consistent degradation（所有5个seed\n      都低于vanilla），LLaMA是intermittent catastrophe（2/3 neutral, 1/3 catastrophic）。\n\n      Reviewer challenge点：(1)\"n=3的SD estimate有极宽CI——单个outlier就能创造4× ratio\"。\n      这是valid的——remove s123后TaxEI SD=0pp。但counter-argument是catastrophic seed\n      本身就是structured injection的核心failure mode。(2)\"LLaMA detection rate 27%\n      vs Qwen 0%——不同architecture在学不同的东西，cross-model comparison的前提被undermined。\"\n      这需要在paper中讨论为architecture-dependent behavior。(3)\"3 seeds on second model\n      is preliminary at best。1/3=33% catastrophic could be 0/10 with more seeds。\"\n\n      Random在LLaMA上mildly beneficial(76.6%>vanilla 73.1%,+3.5pp)——与Qwen(Random=\n      Vanilla degraded)形成对比。这支持\"unstructured noise is benign-to-helpful\"但也\n      表明effect magnitude是model-dependent。Paper必须从\"cross-architecture confirmation\"\n      降级为\"preliminary evidence on two architectures suggesting direction consistency\"。\n\n      Detection rate差异（LLaMA ~27% vs Qwen 0%）是unexpected finding。LLaMA-3.1的\n      instruction-following tendency更强，可能使其more likely to verbalize error awareness\n      即使这种awareness doesn't translate to improved recovery。这实际上strengthens\n      \"detection ≠ recovery\"的argument但需要careful framing。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cross-Model Recovery Rate Comparison\"\n        content: |\n          |              | Qwen3-8B (5-seed)  | LLaMA-3.1-8B (3-seed) |\n          |--------------|:------------------:|:---------------------:|\n          | Vanilla      | 67.3 ± 4.7        | 73.1 ± 2.5           |\n          | TaxEI        | 58.3 ± 6.5        | 69.5 ± 8.6           |\n          | Random       | 58.3 ± 8.7        | 76.6 ± 2.1           |\n          | V−T gap      | −9.0pp             | −3.6pp                |\n          | T SD / R SD  | 0.75×              | 4.1×                  |\n          | Catastrophic | 1/5 (20%)          | 1/3 (33%)             |\n          | Detection    | 0%                 | 27%                   |\n      - name: \"LLaMA Per-Seed Recovery Breakdown\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition       | s42   | s0    | s123       | Mean ± SD     |\n          |-----------------|:-----:|:-----:|:----------:|:-------------:|\n          | Vanilla (rec.)  | 74.5  | 74.5  | 70.2       | 73.1 ± 2.5   |\n          | TaxEI (rec.)    | 74.5  | 74.5  | **59.6**   | 69.5 ± 8.6   |\n          | Random (rec.)   | 74.5  | 76.6  | 78.7       | 76.6 ± 2.1   |\n          | Vanilla (clean) | 72.3  | 72.3  | 72.3       | 72.3 ± 0.0   |\n          | TaxEI (clean)   | 76.6  | 76.6  | **61.7**   | 71.6 ± 8.6   |\n          | Random (clean)  | 74.5  | 76.6  | 76.6       | 75.9 ± 1.2   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart：Qwen 5-seed vs LLaMA 3-seed，V/T/R with error bars。\n         Direction一致（TaxEI最不稳定）但severity profile不同。\"\n      - \"Seed-level dot plot for LLaMA：TaxEI s123 catastrophic outlier突出，\n         Random三点紧密聚集。Annotated with catastrophic threshold line。\"\n      - \"Detection rate comparison bar：Qwen 0% vs LLaMA 27%，分operator。\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLaMA replication是median档的关键升级——将finding从\"single-model negative result\"\n      升级为\"cross-model evidence\"——但3-seed limitation使其只能是preliminary。\n      Direction consistency（TaxEI unstable across both models）是可claim的；\n      magnitude consistency不可claim（Qwen consistent -9pp vs LLaMA intermittent -3.6pp）。\n\n      最大reviewer risk是detection rate差异：如果LLaMA produces 27% detection而Qwen 0%，\n      reviewer会argue the models learn fundamentally different representations from same data，\n      undermining \"cross-model\" claim的validity。Counter：detection doesn't improve recovery\n      (LLaMA TaxEI detection 30% but recovery 69.5% ≈ vanilla 73.1%)，so detection is\n      orthogonal to the stability finding。\n\n      Paper claim wording必须是：\"Structured error injection destabilizes training on\n      both Qwen3-8B (consistent harm, 5-seed) and LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct (intermittent\n      catastrophic failure, 3-seed preliminary), while random injection remains stable\n      across both architectures.\"\n\n  - name: \"Scale Ablation (25K–50K trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-ablation\"\n    description: >\n      将训练数据从~500成功轨迹(4,358 clean samples)扩展至~2,500轨迹(~22K clean samples)，\n      训练V/T/R三条件(3-seed each)。测试TaxEI failure是否primarily due to data scale。\n      ~$44 API + ~54 GPU-h (3-seed×3 conditions with DDP)。\n    expected_results:\n      scaled_vanilla_mean: 71.2\n      scaled_vanilla_sd: 3.5\n      scaled_taxei_mean: 64.8\n      scaled_taxei_sd: 5.2\n      scaled_random_mean: 66.3\n      scaled_random_sd: 4.1\n      gap_taxei_vs_vanilla_pp: -6.4\n      gap_random_vs_vanilla_pp: -4.9\n      gap_taxei_vs_random_pp: -1.5\n      gap_reduction_pct_from_baseline: 29\n      catastrophic_seed_fraction: 0.0\n      training_lottery_range_pp: 12.0\n      cohens_d_scaled: 1.05\n      welch_t_scaled_p: 0.065\n      welch_t_bonferroni_significant: false\n      collection_cost_usd: 44.0\n      unique_tasks_covered: 134\n      trajectories_per_task: 18.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档预测scale-up narrows gap但不eliminate。核心逻辑：\n\n      (1) Vanilla受益最稳定(67.3→71.2%,+3.9pp)：更多clean data直接improve task completion，\n      无conflicting signals。接近ALFWorld的performance ceiling (~75-80% for 8B models)。\n\n      (2) TaxEI gap从-9.0pp缩小至-6.4pp(reduction 29%)：更多data提供更robust的clean\n      signal base，partially buffering against injection noise。但fundamental conflict\n      (structured error patterns vs clean trajectories创造contradictory gradients)不因\n      data volume消失——P2_SubGoalDeletion在任何scale下都会teach \"skip steps is OK\"\n      然后clean data teach \"don't skip steps\"。\n\n      (3) Random gap缩小更多(-9.0→-4.9pp, reduction 46%)：random noise at scale\n      tends to average out(law of large numbers)，而structured patterns maintain\n      systematic bias。这一差异支持\"structured > random for harm\"的claim。\n\n      (4) Catastrophic seed fraction降至0%：5× more data stabilize training dynamics，\n      eliminating the bimodal seed distribution。Training lottery range从19-23pp降至~12pp。\n      这是data scale的genuine positive effect——与\"task structure causes the gap\"不矛盾，\n      因为stability和mean performance是可分离的维度。\n\n      (5) Cohen's d从1.58降至1.05(仍large但approaching medium)，Welch t=0.065(NS)。\n      在median档这意味着：effect real but smaller at scale, still insufficient stat power。\n\n      (6) ALFWorld diversity ceiling：2,500 trajectories ÷ 134 unique tasks = ~19 repetitions/task。\n      PALADIN trains on thousands of unique API patterns。Our \"scale-up\" is actually\n      \"repetition-up\"——Reviewer会correctly identify这个distinction。\n\n      Reviewer典型response：\"The gap narrows 29% at 5× scale, suggesting data volume IS\n      a contributing factor. You cannot claim task structure is the 'primary' cause without\n      matching PALADIN's diversity.\" Median档paper降级claim为：\"Data scale contributes to\n      the failure (29% gap reduction at 5×) but does not fully account for it. The residual\n      6.4pp gap, combined with ALFWorld's 134-task diversity ceiling, points to\n      task-structural differences as a co-dominant factor.\"\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Scale Ablation: 500 vs 2500 Trajectories\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | 500-traj (5s) | 2500-traj (3s) | Δ     | Gap vs V |\n          |-----------|:------------:|:--------------:|:-----:|:--------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 67.3 ± 4.7  | 71.2 ± 3.5    | +3.9  | —        |\n          | TaxEI     | 58.3 ± 6.5  | 64.8 ± 5.2    | +6.5  | −6.4pp   |\n          | Random    | 58.3 ± 8.7  | 66.3 ± 4.1    | +8.0  | −4.9pp   |\n          | Cohen's d | 1.58         | 1.05           | −0.53 | —        |\n          | Catast. % | 20%          | 0%             | elim. | —        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Performance vs log(training_samples) curve for V/T/R。Diminishing returns明显，\n         persistent gap可视化。X轴annotate PALADIN 50K+位置(far right, extrapolated)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale ablation在median档是partial mitigation。Gap减少29%但persist——足以让reviewer\n      同时argue \"scale matters\" AND \"structure matters\"。Paper需要honest framing：\n      \"Increasing data 5× narrows the penalty from 9pp to 6.4pp and eliminates catastrophic\n      seeds, indicating data volume is a contributing factor. The residual gap and\n      ALFWorld's diversity ceiling suggest task structure as a co-dominant factor.\"\n      这是比\"task structure is the primary factor\"弱的claim，但对median档reviewer可接受。\n\n  - name: \"Recovery Prompting (Few-Shot In-Context)\"\n    plan_id: \"recovery-prompting\"\n    description: >\n      Eval时为每个condition提供2/4个in-context recovery examples（展示error→detection→\n      correction序列），测试few-shot能否isolate recovery knowledge vs training signal。\n      如果V/T/R equally benefit，说明recovery能力来自ICL而非SFT。Seed=42, 47 tasks。\n    expected_results:\n      vanilla_0shot_recovery: 61.7\n      vanilla_2shot_recovery: 65.3\n      vanilla_4shot_recovery: 68.1\n      taxei_0shot_recovery: 59.6\n      taxei_2shot_recovery: 63.2\n      taxei_4shot_recovery: 66.0\n      random_0shot_recovery: 63.8\n      random_4shot_recovery: 68.1\n      improvement_vanilla_4shot_pp: 6.4\n      improvement_taxei_4shot_pp: 6.4\n      improvement_random_4shot_pp: 4.3\n      between_condition_4shot_anova_p: 0.78\n      detection_rate_4shot: 0.15\n      detection_rate_0shot: 0.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档预测few-shot prompting universally提升所有条件，无条件间差异。\n\n      (1) ICL provides \"what recovery looks like\" template——是LLM的general能力，\n      与SFT training regime无关。V/T/R同等受益(+4-6pp)证明SFT期间的error injection\n      没有创造任何可被ICL amplify的recovery capability。若TaxEI训练真的teach了latent\n      recovery ability，应该看到TaxEI从few-shot中disproportionately benefit（additive\n      effect: SFT recovery knowledge + ICL recovery template = super-additive）。\n      实际结果：TaxEI improvement = Vanilla improvement = ~6.4pp → zero SFT contribution。\n\n      (2) Detection rate从0%→~15%：ICL examples provide detection template，LLM能\n      模仿format但不reliable执行。这与SFT 0% detection对比：即使explicit error tag\n      exposure during SFT不teach detection，但4个in-context examples partially do。\n      暗示SFT signal在fine-tuning过程中被downstream pattern corruption覆盖，而ICL\n      operates at a more superficial level that preserves detection formatting。\n\n      (3) 4-shot improvement ~5pp mean modest——远低于closing gap to vanilla clean(67.3%)。\n      Even with explicit recovery templates，embodied planning的cascading error nature\n      使genuine recovery fundamentally hard。Models can detect ~15% of errors and still\n      fail to recover from most of them。\n\n      (4) Reviewer视为\"expected given resilience finding\"——如果D041已confirmed\n      resilience-not-recovery，few-shot control是belt-and-suspenders。Value在于\n      completeness而非novelty。Paper中应放Discussion短段而非main result。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Few-Shot Recovery Prompting (seed=42)\"\n        content: |\n          | Condition | 0-shot | 2-shot | 4-shot | Δ(4s−0s) | Det.(4s) |\n          |-----------|:------:|:------:|:------:|:--------:|:--------:|\n          | Vanilla   | 61.7%  | 65.3%  | 68.1%  | +6.4pp   | 14.9%    |\n          | TaxEI     | 59.6%  | 63.2%  | 66.0%  | +6.4pp   | 14.9%    |\n          | Random    | 63.8%  | 66.0%  | 68.1%  | +4.3pp   | 17.0%    |\n          | ANOVA     | —      | —      | F=0.26, p=0.78 | —  | —        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Line plot: shots (0/2/4) × 3 conditions。三条线near-parallel上升，\n         证明improvement is additive-from-ICL而非condition-dependent。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Recovery prompting是clean control but在median档不改变paper narrative。\n      它confirms D041 from a different angle。Paper allocation：Discussion section\n      1段，\"In-context recovery examples provide comparable improvement across all\n      conditions (ANOVA NS), confirming that error injection training does not create\n      latent recovery capacity that can be unlocked by prompting.\"\n\n  - name: \"Per-Operator Deep Dive (Multi-Seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"per-operator-deepdive\"\n    description: >\n      利用recovery-eval-multiseed的5-seed数据，对4个operator分别计算multi-seed\n      TaxEI−Vanilla recovery delta。验证seed=42的local/global gradient是否replicate。\n    expected_results:\n      C4_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: 1.8\n      C4_5seed_sd_pp: 12.5\n      C4_fisher_p: 0.71\n      P1_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -1.2\n      P1_5seed_sd_pp: 10.8\n      P1_fisher_p: 0.82\n      C1_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -3.4\n      C1_5seed_sd_pp: 11.2\n      C1_fisher_p: 0.49\n      P2_5seed_taxei_minus_vanilla_mean_pp: -4.1\n      P2_5seed_sd_pp: 13.1\n      P2_fisher_p: 0.38\n      local_global_gradient_direction_preserved: true\n      local_global_gradient_magnitude_collapsed: true\n      spearman_locality_rank_vs_advantage: 0.60\n      spearman_p: 0.42\n      episodes_per_operator_cell: 57\n    result_rationale: >\n      Median档per-operator gradient在multi-seed后collapse to noise。\n\n      (1) Seed=42的C4=+9.1pp基于11个episodes中1个flip(6→7)——本质上是coin flip。\n      5-seed聚合后~57 episodes/operator/condition给每个operator ~±8-13pp的SD。\n      C4的mean从+9.1→+1.8pp，Fisher p=0.71——signal消失在variance中。\n\n      (2) Direction weakly preserved：local operators(C4)仍slightly positive(+1.8pp)，\n      global operators(C1,P2)仍negative(−3.4, −4.1pp)。但magnitude减小~70%，且\n      Spearman rank correlation(n=4)完全uninformative(p=0.42)。\n\n      (3) P2(sub_goal_deletion)保持最negative(−4.1pp)——合理因为sub-goal deletion是\n      most globally cascading的operator。但Fisher p=0.38 NS，无法distinguish from noise。\n\n      (4) 这个实验的value是将per-operator analysis从\"interesting pattern\"降级为\n      \"hypothesis for future work with larger benchmarks\"。Reviewer会agree这个降级。\n      Paper中从Results Table移至Appendix exploratory analysis。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Operator Recovery Analysis (5-seed)\"\n        content: |\n          | Operator      | Locality | s42 Δ  | 5s Mean Δ | 5s SD   | Fisher p | N/cell |\n          |---------------|:--------:|:------:|:---------:|:-------:|:--------:|:------:|\n          | C4_obs_mask   | Local    | +9.1pp | +1.8pp    | 12.5pp  | 0.71     | ~57    |\n          | P1_step_swap  | Mixed    |  0.0pp | −1.2pp    | 10.8pp  | 0.82     | ~57    |\n          | C1_ctx_trunc  | Global   | −8.3pp | −3.4pp    | 11.2pp  | 0.49     | ~57    |\n          | P2_subgoal_del| Global   | −8.3pp | −4.1pp    | 13.1pp  | 0.38     | ~57    |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Strip plot：每operator每seed一个点(20 points total)，massive scatter，\n         zero line贯穿所有operators。Seed=42用红色标记为outlier-driven。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Per-operator deep dive confirms this analysis is exploratory-only。对paper的impact\n      minimal——main claims不依赖per-operator patterns。Appendix B一页足够。关键句：\n      \"While the directional pattern (local operators neutral, global operators harmful)\n      is consistent with our error cascading hypothesis, per-operator effects are not\n      statistically distinguishable from noise at N≈57 per cell. Benchmarks with >200\n      diverse tasks are needed for per-operator claims.\"\n\n  - name: \"Scale-Up Data Collection (500→2500 Trajectories)\"\n    plan_id: \"scale-up-data\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-5.2 trajectory collection从501扩展至~2,500成功轨迹。分阶段：先1,000 check\n      trend再决定2,500。ALFWorld diversity ceiling ~134 unique tasks。~$44 API cost。\n    expected_results:\n      phase1_1000_trajectories: 1000\n      phase1_1000_cost_usd: 17.6\n      phase1_1000_success_rate: 0.70\n      phase1_1000_unique_tasks: 134\n      phase1_1000_traj_per_task: 7.5\n      phase1_1000_taxei_gap_trend_pp: -7.1\n      phase2_2500_trajectories: 2500\n      phase2_2500_cost_usd: 44.0\n      phase2_2500_traj_per_task: 18.7\n      phase2_2500_samples_clean: 21790\n      phase2_2500_samples_injected: 18400\n      phase2_total_training_time_h: 54\n      phase2_wall_clock_ddp_h: 17\n      diminishing_returns_500_to_1000_gap_reduction_pp: 1.9\n      diminishing_returns_1000_to_2500_gap_reduction_pp: 0.7\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scale-up data collection在median档是feasibility + diminishing returns story。\n\n      (1) Collection feasibility confirmed：70% success rate stable（与initial 501-traj\n      collection一致），cost linear($8.86/500≈$44/2500)。无technical barrier。\n\n      (2) Phase 1 (1,000-traj) gap已经narrow(9.0→7.1pp)，phase 2 (2,500) further\n      narrow(7.1→6.4pp)——clear diminishing returns。500→1000 gains 1.9pp，\n      1000→2500 only 0.7pp。Extrapolating logarithmically，5000 traj would yield\n      ~5.5pp gap——仍non-zero。\n\n      (3) ALFWorld diversity ceiling是fundamental：134 unique tasks × 18.7 repetitions\n      = pure repetition augmentation。PALADIN's advantage可能是task diversity\n      (thousands of unique API call patterns)而非volume。Paper应explicit state：\n      \"Within ALFWorld's 134-task diversity ceiling, data scale reduction accounts for\n      ~29% of the injection penalty. The remaining gap likely reflects task-structural\n      differences that cannot be resolved by repetition-based scaling.\"\n\n      (4) 训练resource significant(54 GPU-h total for 3s×3c)但feasible with 4×5090。\n      Question is ROI：这个experiment对reviewer的说服力是moderate——它addresses\n      concern #10 partially but opens the door for \"you need to scale to 50K\" counter-argument。\n\n      (5) Median档reviewer response：将scale-up result视为evidence for mixed causation\n      (both scale and structure contribute)而非clean separation。这是reasonable——我们\n      不能fully disentangle scale from structure within a single benchmark。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Data Collection Scaling Summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Phase | Traj | Unique Tasks | Traj/Task | Cost  | TaxEI−V Gap | Δ from prev |\n          |-------|:----:|:------------:|:---------:|:-----:|:-----------:|:-----------:|\n          | Base  | 500  | 134          | 3.7       | $8.86 | −9.0pp      | —           |\n          | Ph. 1 | 1000 | 134          | 7.5       | $17.6 | −7.1pp      | +1.9pp      |\n          | Ph. 2 | 2500 | 134          | 18.7      | $44.0 | −6.4pp      | +0.7pp      |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Diminishing returns curve: x=log(trajectories), y=TaxEI−Vanilla gap (pp)。\n         3 data points + logarithmic fit extrapolation to 5K/10K/50K。\n         Annotated PALADIN scale marker at 50K showing gap still projected >0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scale-up data是scale-ablation的prerequisite，结果一致。Diminishing returns\n      是key visual——logarithmic fit shows gap never reaches zero within any feasible\n      ALFWorld scale。This supports task-structure argument but must be presented as\n      \"suggestive projection\" not \"proof\"。\n\n      Paper allocation：Results section一段 + diminishing returns figure。Limitation\n      section承认\"We cannot fully disentangle data scale from task structure within a\n      single benchmark. Cross-benchmark validation (e.g., ToolBench replication of TaxEI)\n      would provide stronger evidence but requires substantial engineering effort.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"30ce2e14-84d3-47ec-abae-17f1dfd2f6a2","total_cost_usd":1.01362025,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53217,"cache_read_input_tokens":118252,"output_tokens":23416,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53217,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":23120,"cache_read_input_tokens":53604,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11060,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11060},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":36308,"outputTokens":32,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.036468,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":23416,"cacheReadInputTokens":118252,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53217,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.97715225,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a99f4b6c-b2e3-4e11-aef7-1fb36505817e"}
